A column renamed: one step, SQLite's own rename. The values follow, and
the database is copied first, as before any step.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup'), (2, 'bread');

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== ledger
ALTER TABLE dish RENAME COLUMN title TO name;

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, ledger.sql's step 1
  step 1
    ALTER TABLE dish RENAME COLUMN title TO name;

== query
SELECT id, name FROM dish ORDER BY id

== rows
1 | soup
2 | bread
